<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-late-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gasterosteus doryssus_late Turing wavelength at 27 µm (9.99 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 78.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg dispersion at r=25 with continuum fastest mode 27.07 µm, a discrete-Laplacian sweep (Pearson r=0.999999, RMSE=0.309 µm), an equal-diffusion ablation (sigma_max=-0.390), and a 12-frame 640x480 ocellus GIF. The GIF is a far-field spiral, not a 2D Schnakenberg field. The 27 µm figure is a detail-scale reconstruction at 9.99 Ma, not a measurement on a Truckee fossil. Overall is intentionally conservative. Overall 78.5/100 (faithfulness 77.3, reproducibility 81.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 82, Morphometric validation 76, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 78, Reproducibility package 80. Output judged: docs/media/gasterosteus_doryssus_late_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-late-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 4032955 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 7a79f832eea0a10c441d64af747767d01f641f64f13c180e0f3ff280d02a05cd (sha256 7a79f832eea0a10c441d64af747767d01f641f64f13c180e0f3ff280d02a05cd), spec_fingerprint 0c1ce9846748ee130d74966458c9300403c6aaed0648f54674b1db5a5f1d5f0e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 0c1ce9846748ee130d74966458c9300403c6aaed0648f54674b1db5a5f1d5f0e; artifact_sha256: 7a79f832eea0a10c441d64af747767d01f641f64f13c180e0f3ff280d02a05cd; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gasterosteus_doryssus_late_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_doryssus_late_specimen.jpg=fd5b18be03310ca2..., datasets/gasterosteus_doryssus_late_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_doryssus_late_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=ba025b0273725b76...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and diffusion-driven instability | Kondo and Miura 2010 treat pigment patterns as reaction-diffusion wavelengths | Hunt, Bell and Travis 2008 document pelvic evolution in a fossil stickleback lineage; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters with r=25 so the continuum fastest mode is 27.07 µm | Du scaled with lambda_m squared across mid (33.62 µm), late (27.07 µm) and marine (21.48 µm) | Far-field spiral used as the late ocellus render; transfer_boundary: 27 µm is the tier-4 detail assignment, not a caliper reading on Truckee material | The gallery plate is an illustrated ocellus card with a 100 µm bar; does_not_claim: Does not claim fossil melanophores were measured at 27 µm | Does not claim the gallery JPEG is a photograph of a Miocene specimen | Does not reuse the 1.7 mm parameters of slot 1209." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Accept the Du sweep as a scored goodness-of-fit: Pearson r and RMSE of discrete versus continuum wavelengths, with value not equal to the 27.07 µm reference.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Score the equal-diffusion ablation (sigma_max and amplitude ratio) as a negative control against the r=25 run.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Segment the gallery plate and the final GIF frame: Sobel-orientation KS and structure-tensor coherency, plus arm spacing measured on the native 640 px frame.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Re-score specimen-match only after the official image-fitness CV similarity of the 12-frame GIF is in hand.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 7.85e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-late-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gasterosteus doryssus_late Turing wavelength at 27 µm (9.99 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Five Du scales move the discrete wavelength monotonically from the marine point through the late point to the mid point. Anisotropy eps moves AP-stripe power from 0.50 (mid) to 0.62 (late) to 0.67 (marine). The sweep is computed, and pass 1 has not yet required it on the figure as a scored morphometric." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
